    the Software or of the applications it manages.
  - Remove or alter any copyright, trademark, or proprietary notices.
  - Use the Software for any purpose that violates applicable law.

4. ACCOUNTS, LICENSES AND APPLICATIONS

Application management, the store, release information and help are
available without an account. Your licenses, purchases, registered
computers and account settings require sign-in.

The sign-in you make in the Software is shared with the Arctisoft
applications on the same Windows user account, so they do not each ask for
it. It is stored on your computer protected by Windows for your user
account.

Premium licenses belong to the individual applications. Their terms,
including the number of computers, the major version covered, trials and
transfers, are those of the License Agreement and of each application's
own agreement. The Software shows and manages those licenses; it does not
change their terms.

Each Arctisoft application can be installed, updated and launched without
the Software.

5. DATA PROCESSING AND PRIVACY

Controller: Arctisoft Studio / Bernd Julian Hagen, Austria,
support@arctisoft-studio.com. The Privacy Policy at
https://arctisoft-studio.com/legal/privacy/ explains your rights under the
GDPR, retention periods and how to complain to a supervisory authority.

Account (when you sign in):

  - Your account email and name, your sign-in methods and authenticator
    settings, your sessions and account activity, and, if you upload one,
    your profile image (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR).
  - Your licenses, orders and purchase records, and the history of license
    transfers (Art. 6(1)(b) and (c) GDPR).
  - Your Studio Hub preferences, such as update checks and automatic
    application updates, so they follow your account.
  - Support requests you send from Help & Support.

Registered computers:

For each computer that uses a license or starts a trial: its name, a
one-way digest of the Windows installation's identifier, a one-way digest
of the hardware identifier its firmware reports, and the IP address at
registration. They apply the limit of computers per license and one trial
per computer (Art. 6(1)(b) and (f) GDPR). They are recorded to apply these
limits, not to track individual user activity.

Payments:

Purchases are processed by Stripe. Arctisoft Studio does not receive or
store your payment card details.

Software updates and releases:

The Software reads Arctisoft Studio's public release feeds on GitHub for
itself and for the applications it manages. These requests carry normal
network information and the version in question, never your files.

The Software has no analytics or telemetry and does not read your personal
files or documents. You can sign out at any time to remove the stored
sign-in from this computer.

You can delete your account in Account & Security. The account closes at
once and is deleted 30 days later; signing in during those 30 days restores
it. Deletion removes your account data as the Privacy Policy describes.
Licenses registered to the account end. Purchase records are retained for
the period required by the Austrian Federal Fiscal Code (BAO, generally
seven years) and then deleted. Uninstalling the Software keeps your
installed applications and does not delete your Arctisoft account.

6. UPDATES

The Software checks for a newer version of itself when it starts. A newer
version is downloaded from the official release repository, verified
against its published checksum and installed before the Software opens;
the start screen shows this.

Whether the Software checks for and installs updates of the Arctisoft
applications is set in Preferences. A version you have pinned is kept.

